  Based on the Sourcegraph deep search, here's the complete picture of tracing patterns in Grafana:
  
  1. Global var tracer = otel.Tracer(...) Pattern: 30 Files

  All 30 files have this anti-pattern. The heaviest concentrations are:
  - pkg/storage/unified/ — 12 files (largest subsystem with this issue)
  - pkg/services/accesscontrol/ — 6 files
  
  Files by package:
  pkg/api/ (1)
  pkg/services/accesscontrol/* (6)
  pkg/services/authz/ (1)
  pkg/services/dashboard* (1)
  pkg/services/frontend/ (1)
  pkg/services/ngalert/ (1)
  pkg/services/notifications/ (1)
  pkg/services/publicdashboards/ (1)
  pkg/services/quota/ (1)
  pkg/services/search/ (1)
  pkg/services/setting/ (1) — special: wrapped variant
  pkg/services/sqlstore/ (1)
  pkg/services/team/ (1)
  pkg/storage/unified/* (12) — the real problem area

  2. Example of Correct Injected Pattern

  From pkg/services/cloudmigration/objectstorage/s3.go:

  type S3 struct {
      httpClient *http.Client
      tracer     tracing.Tracer  // ← field, not global
  func NewS3(httpClient *http.Client, tracer tracing.Tracer) *S3 {
      return &S3{httpClient: httpClient, tracer: tracer}  // ← injected via DI
  }

  func (s3 *S3) PresignedURLUpload(ctx context.Context, ...) error {
      ctx, span := s3.tracer.Start(ctx, "objectstorage.S3.PresignedURLUpload")  // ← uses injected
      defer span.End()
      // ...
  }

  Key benefits:
  - Tracer resolved at constructor time (after SDK initialized)
  - Testable: inject noop.Tracer in tests
  - Follows Wire DI pattern
  - Captures configured SDK, not early global state

  3. Files Mixing Both Patterns?

  No pure mixing found, but one notable variant:

  pkg/services/setting/service.go wraps the global tracer:
  type settingTracer struct {
      trace.Tracer  // wraps OTel tracer
  }

  // Still uses global init at package scope:
  var tracer tracing.Tracer = &settingTracer{otel.Tracer("...")}

  This is a cosmetic improvement (implements tracing.Tracer interface) but still suffers the same timing problem—initialization happens before SDK is configured.

